              <h2>The 7 Best Montessori Apps for Children</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i> Best Subscription-Free Montessori
                      Nature App (Ages 4–10)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> One-Time Purchase (No Subscription)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-earth-americas"></i> Real-World Biomes &amp; Science</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> 100% Offline</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Most Montessori apps focus exclusively on toddler shapes or preschool letter tracing. <strong><a
                      href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong> was created to bring Maria Montessori's vision
                  of <strong>real-world nature, zoology, botany, and geography</strong> to children ages 4–10, without a
                  recurring monthly subscription.
                </p>
                <p>
                  In a completely calm, prepared environment with zero timers, scores, or instructions, children pan
                  across <strong>6 hand-illustrated biomes of the Earth</strong>: the Alps, the African Savannah, the
                  Australian Outback, the Arctic, the Sonoran Desert, and the Amazon Rainforest.
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Discovery Over Instruction:</strong> Kids follow their own curiosity across 120+
                    interactive animals, plants, and geological phenomena, listening to authentic wildlife sounds and
                    observing gentle cause-and-effect animations.</li>
                  <li><strong>~400 Real-World "Did You Know?" Cards:</strong> Tapping the magnifying glass reveals
                    richly illustrated facts in 6 languages (English, Italian, French, German, Spanish, and
                    Portuguese), making them ideal for parent-child co-reading or independent elementary readers.</li>
                  <li><strong>Ethical &amp; Subscription-Free:</strong> Try the app for free, and unlock the entire
                    world forever with a single one-time purchase. 100% offline, zero ads, and zero data tracking.</li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
